 "measures": [
  {
   "name": "Public Measure A (Norwalk School GO Bond)",
   "jurisdiction": "Norwalk Community School District",
   "ballotLanguage": "Shall the Board of Directors of the Norwalk Community School District, in Warren County, State of Iowa, be authorized to contract indebtedness and issue general obligation bonds in an amount not exceeding $65,000,000 for the purpose of acquiring, furnishing, equipping, constructing, improving, repairing, and renovating school buildings and improving the sites of the School District's school buildings and athletic facilities located in Norwalk, Iowa, including without limitation: (a) a new elementary school building and site/land improvements; (b) HVAC system replacement and improvements, kitchen ventilation system improvements, and other mechanical or electrical upgrades to Oviatt Elementary School, Lakewood Elementary School, and Secondary Campus; (c) building improvements and upgrades to enhance security at all existing school buildings, including security systems and enhanced building safety measures; (d) a new transportation building, including maintenance bays, a wash bay, a custodial room, offices, common areas, and site/land improvements; and (e) improving athletic facilities and related parking areas, including construction of a new practice field and building improvements and expansions for additional practice areas, offices, storage space, common areas, and related site improvements?"
  },
  {
   "name": "Public Measure Z (I-35 School GO Bond)",
   "jurisdiction": "Interstate 35 Community School District",
   "ballotLanguage": "Shall the Board of Directors of the Interstate 35 Community School District in the Counties of Clarke, Madison, and Warren, State of Iowa, be authorized to contract indebtedness and issue General Obligation Bonds in an amount not to exceed $12,300,000 to provide funds to remodel, repair, improve, and equip the school building, including reconfiguration of academic spaces, HVAC, mechanical and exterior improvements; to build, furnish, and equip athletic facilities, including a new stadium and track, parking, and site improvements, and for related improvements to repurpose the existing track and field, bleachers, and press box; and for site and access improvements to the school campus?"
  }
 ],
 "notes": "Source: combined official sample ballot PDF (65 ballot styles, text-extractable) plus county candidate list. Board of Supervisors elected by district: District 2 (14 styles) and District 5 (15 styles) are up in 2026; voters see only their own district. Alfonso Valenzuela-Gumucio is listed 'No Party' on the candidate list ('NP' on ballot). Township offices appear only in their township's styles; empty candidate lists are write-in only. Also on the ballot (scope 'special-district'): Greenfield Plaza Water District, Greenfield Plaza/Hills of Coventry Sanitary District, Greenfield Plaza and Hills of Coventry Benefit Light Districts, Lakewood Recreational Lake, and New Virginia Sanitary Sewer trustees. Terms printed on the ballot are kept in 'term'. Measure A appears in 16 styles, Measure Z in 6."
}